-# One line of the packet sheet: what the fact is, its value, and its pencil. The
-# value is the block. It sits in a .fact-value wrapper so opening the inline form
-# hides the whole of it, the unit word included, rather than leaving "seeds" or
-# "days" stranded beside the form.
-# edit is the field type and field for the pencil, or nothing for a fact that
-# is not edited here.
.fact-row{ class: ('text-muted' if local_assigns[:muted]) }
  %dt= label
  %dd
    .fact-value{ class: ("seedfacts--#{display}" if local_assigns[:display]) }= yield
    - if local_assigns[:edit]
      = editable edit.first, seed, edit.last, display_field: ".seedfacts--#{display}", values: local_assigns[:values]
